.nh
.TH "PVEFORGE" "1" "Sep 2026" "pveforge" "pveforge manual"

.SH NAME
pveforge-vm-snapshot-list - List a VM's snapshots, oldest first


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpveforge vm snapshot list <target-id> <vmid> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List a VM's snapshots, oldest first, as one "snapshots" value: each
snapshot's name, snaptime, parent, vmstate and description. PVE's own
"current" entry (the running state) is not a snapshot and is left out.

.PP
Locking: the VM's pveforge lock is held for the whole command (a shared
read lock for list). It serialises pveforge processes only: a change made
at the same time from PVE's web UI or qm is not held off.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--lock-wait\fP=0s
	how long to wait for another pveforge process's lock on this object before giving up (0 = the 15m0s default; at most 1h0m0s). The default exceeds the 10m0s ceiling on waiting for a PVE task because a legitimate lock holder may be in such a wait the whole time

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="kv"
	output format: "kv" or "json"

.PP
\fB--roster\fP=""
	path to the roster file (overrides PVEFORGE_ROSTER and the default ./pveforge.toml)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpveforge-vm-snapshot(1)\fP
